the Hyperion cantos is a series of four  science fiction novels written by Dan  Simmons the story takes place hundreds  of years in our future at a time where  humankind has formed the hegemony  spreading out to many planets mankind  also now had the technology to instantly  travel from any world connected in the  far casting web the books mainly centre  however on the far off planet of  Hyperion where the merciless strike  resides the creature known as the strike  in the Hyperion cantos is one of the  most intriguing characters to come out  of modern science fiction the creature  which was named for the carnivorous  passerine birds of Old Earth terrorizes  the world of Hyperion the Shrike is a  being of mysterious origin an incredible  power the Shrike appeared in the books  as four armed and vaguely humanoid its  entire body was comprised of some  strange metal similar to steel with  countless barbs and spikes covering it  throughout the series the shrikes goals  and motivations are ambiguous it seems  to act with no rhyme or reason the  Shrike first appeared on Hyperion with  the arrival of the time tombs six  strange structures in a distant Valley  on the world the time tombs were  constructed at some point in the distant  future and were sent hurtling backwards  through time it is assumed early on that  the Shrike itself was also created at  some point in the distant future but for  an unknown purpose on the planet  Hyperion the being called the Shrike  impales its victims upon the tree of  pain a giant structure made of a similar  material to the creature itself impaled  upon the spikes of the shrikes tree its  victims would be condemned to suffer  eternally fully conscious and aware of  their own agony the strikes victims  could potentially numb  the millions the Shrike had the power to  move through the void which binds in  order to travel through time and space  it could travel anywhere but for the  vast majority of its existence it chose  to reside solely on the planet Hyperion  in a territory that it had chosen the  Shrike could move so fast that it often  appeared to be in two places at once and  its many thorns and spikes could easily  butcher any opponent it faced normal  weapons had no effect on the striking  and the creature often intentionally  chose to mutilate its opponents and  exceedingly horrifying and painful ways  perhaps due to the ambiguity of its  origins and due to the godlike power of  the Shrike the Church of the final  atonement was formed after the Shrike  first appeared on Hyperion the Shrike  church revered the entity naming it the  Lord of pain many within the Galactic  hegemony believed the church to be a  cult the Church believes that one day  the Shrike will unleash its rage unto  the inhabited worlds of the galaxy and  punished the living for the sins of  mankind it is suggested in the later  books that the strike may have been the  final result of something that evolved  alongside the technic or the entity  created through the amalgamation of all  sentient artificial intelligence it was  called the reaper program the reaper  program was originally designed to  maintain order amongst the first AIS and  as the eons passed and the AI is formed  into the Technic or the reaper program  continuously grew and evolved as well  eventually creating the Shrike the  Shrike acted as the Avatar to the old  intelligence an AI god created by the  techno core in the distant future it had  known true motive of its own it is  somewhat in flight that the strike had  been sent back in time to seek out the  human counterpart to the ultimate  intelligence which was the collected  conscience of humanity the ultimate  human intelligence would reside  somewhere in the void which binds it is  possible that the strikes tree of  painting was intended to draw out the  human intelligence so that the strike  could eliminate it before it was ever a  threat to its AI equivalent the strike  is of key importance in the Hyperion  cantos it appears in each of the four  novels and is a part of every major  character arc in the series
 

